# MX3-2 write-up B: GEMM operands through a shared-memory ring (ldg_b128_bsm).
# Apply with git apply; enable with -DTILEMEGA_SMEM_RING_BYTES=<bytes>.
# Body tests (test/python/test_mx_task_bodies.py) pass with the ring at 16384 bytes
# once the test launches allocate at least that much shared memory (2026-10-22).
# Inside the serving megakernel, mxcc (MACA 3.8.2.6) did not finish: 30 min at
# 16384 bytes and 25 min at 8192 bytes on the Qwen3-0.6B B1 plan, killed by
# timeout; the same code compiles in 25 s in the body-test library.
# With the macro at 0 the patch still changes GemmStageTaskBody's machine code
# (4549 -> 4585 instructions), so it is kept out of the default build.
